From 69902fc83cdca04c887b4f1f59d244727e924d03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:27:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 056/108] gpu: vulkan: experimental resolve feed into cached
 textures (off by default)

A 1x k_8_8_8_8 resolve written bitwise into an up-to-date cached texture of
the same format, endianness and pitch (single level, single slice) is copied
straight from the render target into the texture (vkCmdCopyImage, added to
the deferred command buffer and the device function table), and the texture
stays valid instead of being reloaded from guest memory, as Lost Odyssey's
renderer keeps resolved images on the GPU. Guest memory is still written.
Off by default (vulkan_resolve_feed_textures): Lightning Returns' resolves
all swap red and blue, which an image copy can't do, so it never applies
there yet and is unverified on hardware. Logs the first reasons a resolve
can't feed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

